      "project": "R4Basic",
      "name": "R4BASIC",
      "role": "Subsystem",
      "kind": "R4X",
      "artifact": "R4BASIC.R4X",
      "image_scope": "full",
      "path": "Repositories/Subsystems/R4Basic",
      "notes": "SUBSYSTEM_ID=r4os.basic; GUEST_FORMAT=basic.qbasic-source; module 1.2.32 and final contract 2.10.2. One parser-binder-emitter and a mandatory all-green catalog gate cover seven Part-1 fundamentals, all 193 Part-2 statements/functions, three metacommands and 43 Appendix-B errors. The permanent general positive/negative/runtime corpus and checksum-bound unchanged GORILLA full-round/reset/close acceptance cover source graphs, numerics, strings, declarations, procedures, files, R4OS platform semantics, all logical SCREEN modes, graphics, audio and events. The productive guest baseline additionally requires real intro PCM and a successful idle Close after the documented AUDSVC/HDA drain; 50-ms Open/Write/Volume and separate 500-ms Close bounds cover the verified four-CPU service latency, while degradation reports per-operation counters. Newly consumed sequence-tagged console input publishes its echo in the same guest slice and restarts the 33-ms cadence; non-input deferred frames retain their own guest wake deadline. Physical key transitions remain deliberately outside BASIC semantics. An exact private 1-MiB 20-bit machine provides guest pointers, bounded x86, ports, virtual interrupts and private foreign symbols; bounded COM/IOCTL and printer spools never expose host hardware. Retains one-outstanding-request bounded storage, event-driven waits, 262144-operation/8-ms slices, generation-safe Indexed8 presentation and full instance isolation."
    },
    {
      "project": "R4GB",
      "name": "R4GB",
      "role": "Subsystem",
      "kind": "R4X",
      "artifact": "R4GB.R4X",
      "image_scope": "full",
