      "notes": "SUBSYSTEM_ID=r4os.gb; GUEST_FORMAT=gameboy.dmg-cartridge; module 0.10.7. Original userland DMG implementation with explicit CPU revision profiles and no proprietary boot ROM. Complete owned-ROM validation, full-ROM SHA-256 identity, bounded 64-KiB bus and ROM-only/MBC1/MBC1M/MBC2/MBC3/MBC30/MBC5/MMM01/digital-HuC1 models provide the cartridge foundation; hardware-bound mapper and accessory families are rejected precisely. Battery cartridges persist exact raw SRAM and versioned checksummed MBC3 RTC state below C:\\R4OS\\SUBSYSTEMS\\r4os.gb\\SAVE using the compiled-in shared SDK persistence helper: one generation-bound writer lease and an asynchronous serial snapshot worker with coalescing, same-directory atomic replacement, bounded retries for transient stream not-found/I/O faults across stage and private transaction-lease Begin/Write/Finish, ownership-aware Abort/Release retries, checked normal transaction release, bounded replay of retained stages after interrupted or lost-acknowledgement writes, exact-size and RTC-content validation before replay, last-good backup preservation until the canonical target is independently resolvable and validated, and mandatory drain-on-close; partial or malformed stages and orphaned backups fail closed, the former pre-release APPDATA path is never probed at runtime, and the one affected laptop installation was restored byte-identically before activation; non-battery cartridges never persist. The source migration retains R4GB's cartridge and 80-byte RTC policy and introduces neither an R4L nor a platform ABI. The complete SM83 core covers all 244 legal base and 256 CB paths through explicit read/write/idle M-cycles. One bounded 4.194304-MHz Machine clock owns DIV/TIMA reload behavior, IF/IE priority and dispatch retargeting, HALT/STOP wake, 160-byte OAM DMA with restart and DMG source decoding, the active-low P1 keyboard matrix, deterministic SB/SC transfer without link transport and the MBC3 RTC across CPU halt/stop